===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*megʰ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|mayn}}, {{m|enm|main}}, {{m|enm|maine}}, {{m|enm|mæin}}, {{m|enm|meyn}}, from {{m|enm|main|pos=noun}} (''see further'' at [[#Etymology 2|etymology 2]]); compare {{inh|en|ang|mæġen||strong, main, principal}} {{qualifier|used in combination}}<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=main|pos=adj|id=MED26523|accessdate=3 June 2018}}</ref> and {{der|en|non|megn}}, {{m|non|megenn||strong, main}}.

The word is cognate with {{cog|goh|megīn||strong, mighty}} (modern {{cog|de|Möge}}, {{m|de|Vermögen||power, wealth}}), and also akin to {{cog|ang|magan||to be able to}}. ''See also'' {{m|en|may}}.

